MID_EV13_064_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_064_m01_001: My tale begins long ago, centuries before you\nwere born.
MID_EV13_064_m01_002: There was a desert then, and in that desert was a\nwhite egg. Many people lived peacefully within it.
MID_EV13_064_m01_003: Until one day, when the dragon called Dagda the\nGreat struck and cracked the desert egg.
MID_EV13_064_m01_004: The peace was shattered. The People of the White\nEgg took up arms against the empire and its dragon.
MID_EV13_064_m01_005: They warred and lost. The empire brought them in\nchains to its capital.
MID_EV13_064_m01_006: And then, Auntie Troy? What happened to the\npeople after that?
MID_EV13_064_m01_007: The empire's prisoners came to a tragic end.
MID_EV13_064_m01_008: Those who were taken were put to death, boiled\nalive in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV13_064_m01_009: But the goddess Yu Phas saw all. Her heart ached to\nsee them treated that way.
MID_EV13_064_m01_010: And so she rescued five thousand children of the\nWhite Egg.
MID_EV13_064_m01_011: They grew up to found the kingdom of Damascar.\nThose children are your ancestors.
MID_EV13_064_m01_012: That story was too scary, Auntie. Why did you tell it\nto me?
MID_EV13_064_m01_013: Because it is true. Your people must never forget\nyour history.
MID_EV13_064_m01_014: But why did Dagda the Great want to kill all the\negg people?
MID_EV13_064_m01_015: Deep down, child, he feared them.
MID_EV13_064_m01_016: That doesn't make sense. Dagda is lots scarier!
MID_EV13_064_m01_017: I hate all the gods of the temples, except Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_064_m01_018: Auntie? What was Yu Phas like?
MID_EV13_064_m01_019: Was she kind and pretty and wonderful?
MID_EV13_064_m01_020: Yes and yes and yes. She was all of those things.
MID_EV13_064_m01_021: What?! You knew her, Auntie?! No fair!
MID_EV13_064_m01_022: Yu Phas is the goddess of the underworld, right?\nWill I get to meet her when I die?
MID_EV13_064_m01_023: The living need not be concerned with what may\ncome after death.
MID_EV13_064_m01_024: To be human is to live with all one's strength until\nthe final moments, no matter the circumstances.
MID_EV13_064_m01_025: Always ask yourself until the very end, Theodora,\nif you are living to your true purpose.
MID_EV13_064_m01_026: Even if the question goes unanswered, that is what\nit means to live with all one's strength.
MID_EV13_064_m01_027: I don't understand, Auntie. You're confusing me.
MID_EV13_064_m01_028: Think of it this way, then.
MID_EV13_064_m01_029: Wouldn't Yu Phas be sad if you didn't live with all\nyour strength, after she saved your ancestors?
MID_EV13_064_m01_030: Mmmm...
MID_EV13_064_m01_031: Theodora? What's wrong, child?
MID_EV13_064_m01_032: Yu Phas had such a good heart. I hate that she had\nto die.
MID_EV13_064_m01_033: When I'm older, I want to be strong so I can save\npeople like Yu Phas did.
MID_EV13_064_m01_034: I'll protect everyone. I'll be so strong...that no\none can...
MID_EV13_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_000_m01_001: It is good to see you again, Kumos, especially after\nour long absence.
MID_EV13_000_m01_002: Three years is quite a tour of duty. I bet you're glad\nto be back here rather than stuck at Fort Zanbar.
MID_EV13_000_m01_003: We regretted to hear of your skirmish with the Mosa\ntoward the end of your stay.
MID_EV13_000_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him it was dangerous.
MID_EV13_000_m01_005: <NCB>Tell him it was nothing.
MID_EV13_000_m01_006: <ACA>Indeed. Had we departed slightly earlier, they may\nhave posed a real threat.
MID_EV13_000_m01_007: <ACA>As it was, they struck during the overlap between the\nrelief commander's arrival and our own departure.
MID_EV13_000_m01_008: <ACA>Though one hopes never to face an invasion, this one\nwas timed ideally for us to quell it.
MID_EV13_000_m01_009: <ACB>Would that every foe could be dealt with so easily.
MID_EV13_000_m01_010: <ACB>It's always a privilege to watch the boss in action.\nI'd hate to be in the other guy's shoes!
MID_EV13_000_m01_011: <ACB>After a rout like that, the Mosa will think twice\nbefore sticking their necks out again.
MID_EV13_000_m01_012: Fort Zanbar is as important strategically to Saramis\nas Grania's Waist.
MID_EV13_000_m01_013: The Mosa would no doubt love to seize it if\nthey could.
MID_EV13_000_m01_014: It is undeniable that the Mosa have lately been\nemboldened to act.
MID_EV13_000_m01_015: Our return to Megaira sits uneasily with me.
MID_EV13_000_m01_016: Unfortunately, Princess, the people of your kingdom\nneed you here.
MID_EV13_000_m01_017: Once Your Highness comes into adulthood, you will\nsit on the Saramis throne.
MID_EV13_000_m01_018: So this is an important ceremony for our\nkingdom's future.
MID_EV13_000_m01_019: I am relieved that Your Highness returned in time\nfor your twentieth birthday.
MID_EV13_000_m01_020: And of course, King Sergio has been eager to see his\ndaughter again.
MID_EV13_000_m01_021: I see. And how does my father fare?
MID_EV13_000_m01_022: His condition seems stable. Troy's medicine is\nworking its usual wonders.
MID_EV13_000_m01_023: Good. Now, I have been away from Megaira too\nlong. I shall visit Father once I feel settled again.
MID_EV13_000_m01_024: One last thing, Your Highness.
MID_EV13_000_m01_025: Your younger brother, Prince Dyan, has been acting\nsomewhat...erratically.
MID_EV13_000_m01_026: The reports say he was gone from Megaira for some\ntime. He returned only a few days ago.
MID_EV13_000_m01_027: So noted. I will be vigilant. Please let me know if\nanything else requires my attention.
MID_EV13_000_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}That's right...settle in. Enjoy this moment before your\nworld becomes an unending hell.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_000_m01_029: {SetColor=Gray}The sight of your tears will be exquisite,\nmy dear sister.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_001_m01_001: Nghhh...
MID_EV13_001_m01_002: I implore you, Your Highness...try to keep a\nbrave face.
MID_EV13_001_m01_003: My weakness is to blame for Father's death.
MID_EV13_001_m01_004: The people of Saramis are pioneers. Their ruler must\nbe capable of wielding the Monarch's Axe.
MID_EV13_001_m01_035: If I cannot hold it aloft during the coronation\nceremony, my claim to the throne is invalid.
MID_EV13_001_m01_036: Such is the way of the forest peoples—a tradition\nmaintained since the kingdom of Damascar.
MID_EV13_001_m01_005: Our laws are very clear on that point. I... I am no\nlonger eligible to be queen.
MID_EV13_001_m01_037: Couldn't you...I dunno...just put your back into it?
MID_EV13_001_m01_038: Do not be absurd, Tobias.
MID_EV13_001_m01_039: Even Her Highness would find it impossible to wield\nthat particular axe one-handed.
MID_EV13_001_m01_006: Oh, my dear sister. You look ghastly.
MID_EV13_001_m01_007: Dyan?
MID_EV13_001_m01_008: Prince Dyan. By your leave, Princess Theodora\nmust rest now.
MID_EV13_001_m01_009: Silence, Bonaventure! It is not given to you to\nchastise me.
MID_EV13_001_m01_010: Ah— Pardon, I...
MID_EV13_001_m01_011: I heard that something dreadful had happened and\ncame to see what it was. Is that so wrong?
MID_EV13_001_m01_012: Am I not permitted to ask after my own sibling?\nWhere is the harm in that?
MID_EV13_001_m01_013: And now I hear that our father is dead—thanks to\nyou, my dear sister. Such a disgraceful affair.
MID_EV13_001_m01_014: <NCA>Scowl at Dyan.
MID_EV13_001_m01_015: <NCB>Avert your eyes.
MID_EV13_001_m01_016: <ACA>That is— No.
MID_EV13_001_m01_017: I can offer no excuse. I was there and yet failed to\ncapture the villain.
MID_EV13_001_m01_018: Had I been stronger, I could have won out despite\nthe confusion of the moment.
MID_EV13_001_m01_019: Too true. What is your strength for if not to protect a\nsingle person—our own father—from harm? Pathetic.
MID_EV13_001_m01_020: Perhaps matters would have played out differently\nhad I been the one defending him...
MID_EV13_001_m01_021: You two-faced snake!
MID_EV13_001_m01_022: They laud you as the Iron Bastion in the south, but\nyou haven't lived up to that reputation here, hm?
MID_EV13_001_m01_023: Perhaps it's something to do with the arm you're\nkeeping under that cloak?
MID_EV13_001_m01_024: Let's have a look. Show your brother what ails you.
MID_EV13_001_m01_025: You wouldn't hide anything from me, would you?
MID_EV13_001_m01_026: Mmph...
MID_EV13_001_m01_027: No need, of course. I already know. Why, the whole\npalace is abuzz with the news.
MID_EV13_001_m01_028: How the poor princess lost her dominant arm to\na base villain.
MID_EV13_001_m01_029: He even carried the unsightly thing off as he fled!
MID_EV13_001_m01_030: And with it, my dear sister, he took the last hope of\nyou ever claiming the throne.
MID_EV13_001_m01_031: Meaning that I, Dyan Sergio Savangren, will be\nthe next king of Saramis!
MID_EV13_001_m01_032: And my first act as king will be to banish you\nfrom Megaira.
MID_EV13_001_m01_033: Though if you bow and scrape to my liking, I may\nmerely confine you to the inner palace.
MID_EV13_001_m01_034: Hyahaha... HYAHAHA!
MID_EV13_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_002_m01_001: That marks the last of the arrangements for the\nroyal funeral.
MID_EV13_002_m01_002: Thank you for all you have done, Chancellor.\nThere are not enough hours in the day for it.
MID_EV13_002_m01_003: Don't concern yourself on my behalf. There are\ngreater things at stake.
MID_EV13_002_m01_004: I fear for my beloved Saramis.
MID_EV13_002_m01_005: Bona! Mos! We've got a serious problem!
MID_EV13_002_m01_006: The boss has up and disappeared! I've been all over\nthe palace, and I can't find her anywhere!
MID_EV13_002_m01_007: Not so loud, you fool! Guard your tongue.
MID_EV13_002_m01_008: Anyone in this palace may be a turncoat.
MID_EV13_002_m01_009: I don't believe this. Where could Princess Theodora\nhave gone in her condition?!
MID_EV13_002_m01_010: You don't think she...y'know...went to fall on her\nsword somewhere?
MID_EV13_002_m01_011: The princess? Never! Come, let us find her before\nyet another disaster strikes.
MID_EV13_002_m01_012: I suggest we assemble a search party of trusted\ncourtiers. What say you, Kumos?
MID_EV13_002_m01_013: R-right you are. I'll see to it at once!
MID_EV13_002_m01_014: So she's vanished...and the chancellor's faction is\nwasting no time locating her.
MID_EV13_002_m01_015: Have they forgotten already? She's an ordinary\nwoman now, not the next in line for the throne.
MID_EV13_002_m01_016: Her only redeeming quality was her beastly strength,\nand that went out with her arm.
MID_EV13_002_m01_017: Just what will they do if they find her? There isn't a\nshred of support for her claim.
MID_EV13_002_m01_018: Hmmm...
MID_EV13_002_m01_019: And yet...caution may be called for.
MID_EV13_002_m01_020: You summoned me, Prince Dyan?
MID_EV13_002_m01_021: The chancellor and his faction are up to something.\nA wasted effort, to be sure, but still.
MID_EV13_002_m01_022: Have some of your cohort keep eyes on them.\nOh, and get word to him...
MID_EV13_002_m01_023: Bahr Vahn, chief of the Har Hali, that is—the man\nwho took my sister's arm.
MID_EV13_002_m01_024: Is that wise, my prince? He is a dangerous one\nto associate with.
MID_EV13_002_m01_025: You forget yourself, Huver, when you question the\nwisdom of the next king of Saramis.
MID_EV13_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_003_m01_001: I'm sorry, Theodora, but this is beyond my skill.\nIf you at least still had the severed arm...
MID_EV13_003_m01_002: What I ask is absurd, and yet I ask it anyway.\nI must have a new arm, Troy.
MID_EV13_003_m01_003: Surely this is not impossible for you! Not for a\nsurvivor of the White Egg!
MID_EV13_003_m01_035: I would offer anything rather than give up now.
MID_EV13_003_m01_004: Before that, I must tell you of a strange rumor\nI heard. You will not like what it suggests.
MID_EV13_003_m01_005: They say that a noble of Saramis was seen keeping\ncompany with Bahr Vahn of the Har Hali.
MID_EV13_003_m01_006: <NCA>Muse about the assailant.
MID_EV13_003_m01_007: <NCB>Muse about Dyan.
MID_EV13_003_m01_008: <ACA>The intruder was unknown to me. I found myself at\na loss in the face of his skill.
MID_EV13_003_m01_009: <ACA>The Har Hali are experts with the blade. It seems\nplausible that you encountered one of them.
MID_EV13_003_m01_010: So Dyan pulled these strings. If he stooped to\npatricide, then he is rotten to the heart!
MID_EV13_003_m01_011: But as to your question...long ago, a warrior of the\nforest peoples lost an arm, much like you.
MID_EV13_003_m01_012: Yet this one-armed warrior, known as Mahadu,\nwas the strongest of his people.
MID_EV13_003_m01_013: In his case, as in yours, the laws handed down from\nDamascar prevented him from leadership.
MID_EV13_003_m01_014: But then, a spirit of the land blessed him with\na powerful new arm.
MID_EV13_003_m01_015: Mahadu swiftly unified the local clans and\nbrought them all into a single people.
MID_EV13_003_m01_016: They were the people of Saramis, predecessors to\nyour kingdom of Saramis.
MID_EV13_003_m01_017: I know the legend. Mahadu is the ancestor of the\nSaramis royal family, after all.
MID_EV13_003_m01_018: His axe could split a guibouga tree in half, and his\nsword could calm the stormiest sea.
MID_EV13_003_m01_019: Some say that a spear he threw pierced a boulder—\nand still took the heads of three warriors after.
MID_EV13_003_m01_036: If the legend is true, that arm could make me capable\nof lifting the Monarch's Axe.
MID_EV13_003_m01_020: However...five years with the arm took a toll on his\nmind. For the arm was a blessing but also a curse.
MID_EV13_003_m01_021: After 10 years with it, he vanished entirely.\nAnd that was that.
MID_EV13_003_m01_022: Troy...you know, don't you?
MID_EV13_003_m01_023: You know where Mahadu rests, where I can find\nthe arm the spirit blessed him with.
MID_EV13_003_m01_024: I do, yes. But hear me, Theodora.
MID_EV13_003_m01_025: Power that great comes at a cost. The arm's curse\nis something no one should suffer.
MID_EV13_003_m01_026: Even should you use it to become queen, it will do\nyou little good when you lose your mind.
MID_EV13_003_m01_027: I do not think this is what your father would have\nwanted for you.
MID_EV13_003_m01_028: That arm bested the likes of Mahadu. You will get\nno more than the 10 years he had.
MID_EV13_003_m01_029: The law that forbids you from the throne still leaves\nyou the rank of commander, yes?
MID_EV13_003_m01_030: You are beloved by the people. Perhaps you could\nfind a proxy and inspire a faction to resist...
MID_EV13_003_m01_031: <NCA>Deny her.
MID_EV13_003_m01_032: If Dyan becomes king, I will be exiled at once.\nThere is no time for what you suggest.
MID_EV13_003_m01_033: I beseech you, Troy. Tell me where I can find\nMahadu's arm.
MID_EV13_003_m01_034: Very well... I will tell you what I know.
MID_EV13_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_004_m01_001: Your death is certain, Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_004_m01_002: Your soldiers are vanquished. Know that there is no\npath left to you.
MID_EV13_004_m01_003: That right arm of yours... Do I recognize the spirit\narm of Mahadu?
MID_EV13_004_m01_004: So there was truth behind the legend. In that case...\nI want it.
MID_EV13_004_m01_005: Its power intrigues me.
MID_EV13_004_m01_006: The next time we meet, I will take the arm for\nmyself. Remember that.
MID_EV13_004_m01_007: There will be no next time. For the vile crime of\nmurdering my father, you will die here and now.
MID_EV13_004_m01_008: Just so. It seems uncouth to do this before the tomb\nof a great hero, but so be it.
MID_EV13_004_m01_009: There's three of us and one of you. You can't run.
MID_EV13_004_m01_010: Grr...
MID_EV13_004_m01_011: Watch it, boss! I don't like that glint in his eye!
MID_EV13_004_m01_012: Rah!
MID_EV13_004_m01_013: Rrrrgh!
MID_EV13_004_m01_014: I've taken your left hand as equal measure for my\nright arm.
MID_EV13_004_m01_015: But the scales are not balanced yet. You've more to\npay for your sins.
MID_EV13_004_m01_016: The next thing I take from you will be your head.
MID_EV13_004_m01_017: Rrgh...
MID_EV13_004_m01_018: Oomph.
MID_EV13_004_m01_019: Get back, boss!
MID_EV13_004_m01_020: Chief! Quick, over here!
MID_EV13_004_m01_021: Did we not get them all?!
MID_EV13_004_m01_022: <NCA>Survey the situation.
MID_EV13_004_m01_023: Grrr...
MID_EV13_004_m01_024: He's gone. I had hoped to make an end of it here.
MID_EV13_004_m01_025: A Har Hali warrior, eh? His mettle was formidable.
MID_EV13_004_m01_026: He's one of them, alright. Might be the toughest of all\nthe forest clans.
MID_EV13_004_m01_027: Buncha Balor worshippers, the lot of 'em.
MID_EV13_004_m01_028: I mean, sure, Balor is Yu Phas's dad and all, but...
MID_EV13_004_m01_029: I don't want any part of a god like him.
MID_EV13_004_m01_030: Bahr Vahn of the Har Hali...
MID_EV13_004_m01_031: I pray that losing him here does not spell disaster\nlater on.
MID_EV13_004_m01_032: Mmm.